title: Help Desk Impersonation Followed by Portable Runtime and Renamed Rclone
id: 0a11e366-a403-43b5-9543-cbacd0992f36
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the post-Quick-Assist tradecraft Microsoft documented in the ESC1
    and ESC8 intrusions: portable Python, Bun, or Java runtimes staged in
    KB-prefixed directories under the user profile, and a renamed Rclone
    binary (SearchApp.exe) used to copy data to an external SFTP destination.
references:
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/
    - https://specterops.io/blog/2021/06/17/certified-pre-owned/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/03
tags:
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1048
    - attack.t1649
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_portable_runtime:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\bun.exe'
            - '\java.exe'
            - '\python.exe'
            - '\python3.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - '\AppData\Roaming\KB'
    selection_renamed_rclone:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\SearchApp.exe'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'sftp:'
            - ' copy '
    condition: selection_portable_runtime or selection_renamed_rclone
falsepositives:
    - Developer tooling that runs portable runtimes from a KB-prefixed profile directory
    - Legitimate Rclone deployments renamed for packaging (validate the parent process and destination)
level: medium
